|\\cdot ‖v‖ \\\\  & =4\\sqrt{{v}_{1}^{2}+{v}_{2}^{2}+{v}_{3}^{2}+{v}_{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =4\\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+{3}^{2}+{1}^{2}+(-3)^{2}} \\\\  & =4\\sqrt{1+9+1+9} \\\\  & =4\\sqrt{20} \\\\  & =4\\cdot 2\\sqrt{5} \\\\  & =8\\sqrt{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-dfbc77cc-9928-5c7b-a442-680cf76c0925"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-dfbc77cc-9928-5c7b-a442-680cf76c0925" :answer-field/id #uuid "dfbc77cc-9928-5c7b-a442-680cf76c0925" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-b37fbc05-fe82-5876-bcb9-d58736c4f50d" :answer-field/choices ["answer-8ab3596c-42f0-561d-978c-86dd4ffe5fc4" "answer-ab701453-cfdc-5ae4-b243-b1e4e6c6f06d" "answer-09cd35ab-5375-5955-b3eb-b86578cb2956" "answer-bebae5b0-873f-5d88-8b25-daff30c6fafa" "answer-b37fbc05-fe82-5876-bcb9-d58736c4f50d"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8ab3596c-42f0-561d-978c-86dd4ffe5fc4" :answer/id #uuid "8ab3596c-42f0-561d-978c-86dd4ffe5fc4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2\\sqrt{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ab701453-cfdc-5ae4-b243-b1e4e6c6f06d" :answer/id #uuid "ab701453-cfdc-5ae4-b243-b1e4e6c6f06d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\sqrt{10}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-09cd35ab-5375-5955-b3eb-b86578cb2956" :answer/id #uuid "09cd35ab-5375-5955-b3eb-b86578cb2956" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4\\sqrt{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bebae5b0-873f-5d88-8b25-daff30c6fafa" :answer/id #uuid "bebae5b0-873f-5d88-8b25-daff30c6fafa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8\\sqrt{10}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b37fbc05-fe82-5876-bcb9-d58736c4f50d" :answer/id #uuid "b37fbc05-fe82-5876-bcb9-d58736c4f50d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "8\\sqrt{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186134239 :question/problem "If $‖3x‖=4$, find $‖\\frac{x}{5}‖.$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that we can factor a constant out of the norm, provided that we take the absolute value of the constant:\n\n$$\n‖kx‖=|k|\\cdot ‖x‖\n$$\n\nUsing this fact, we can solve for the norm $‖x‖$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖3x‖ & =4 \\\\ |3|\\cdot ‖x‖ & =4 \\\\ ‖x‖ & =\\frac{4}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can evaluate $‖\\frac{x}{5}‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖\\frac{x}{5}‖ & =\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot ‖x‖ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\cdot \\frac{4}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{15}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186131473 :answer-field/correct 17592186131476 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "question-107fc4e1-2e72-5e57-99ba-69f5d3ed0685" :question/id #uuid "107fc4e1-2e72-5e57-99ba-69f5d3ed0685" :question/math-academy-id "q-139967" :question/problem "Given the vector $v=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -6 \\\\ \\sqrt{74}\\end{aligned}]$, find $‖2v‖.$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that we can factor a constant out of the norm, provided that we take the absolute value of the constant:\n\n$$\n‖kv‖=|k|\\cdot ‖v‖\n$$\n\nUsing this fact and the formula for the norm, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖2v‖ & =|2|\\cdot ‖v‖ \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{{v}_{1}^{2}+{v}_{2}^{2}+{v}_{3}^{2}+{v}_{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{(-3)^{2}+{5}^{2}+(-6)^{2}+(\\sqrt{74})^{2}} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{9+25+36+74} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{144} \\\\  & =2\\cdot 12 \\\\  & =24.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-b4403c4d-563f-5e8f-aca5-9ab394c3e8dd"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-b4403c4d-563f-5e8f-aca5-9ab394c3e8dd" :answer-field/id #uuid "b4403c4d-563f-5e8f-aca5-9ab394c3e8dd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-ffe1ccce-1e77-544c-b011-efa06b2a02bf" :answer-field/choices ["answer-ffe1ccce-1e77-544c-b011-efa06b2a02bf"