[:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-a1b99505-88f3-5e64-abac-1b95f853d681" :answer-field/id #uuid "a1b99505-88f3-5e64-abac-1b95f853d681" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-939ab4ac-b0eb-5583-a507-30ec715ed593" :answer-field/choices ["answer-741632d1-208c-5d04-9dd7-95fb12ced8dc" "answer-21569f32-2dd3-522d-a835-82a75760b312" "answer-20baf338-65e1-5d1d-b674-3f0a7f87c7ae" "answer-4299f0c5-cc63-5808-99df-fdda4a65c6fb" "answer-939ab4ac-b0eb-5583-a507-30ec715ed593"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-741632d1-208c-5d04-9dd7-95fb12ced8dc" :answer/id #uuid "741632d1-208c-5d04-9dd7-95fb12ced8dc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-21569f32-2dd3-522d-a835-82a75760b312" :answer/id #uuid "21569f32-2dd3-522d-a835-82a75760b312" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-20baf338-65e1-5d1d-b674-3f0a7f87c7ae" :answer/id #uuid "20baf338-65e1-5d1d-b674-3f0a7f87c7ae" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4299f0c5-cc63-5808-99df-fdda4a65c6fb" :answer/id #uuid "4299f0c5-cc63-5808-99df-fdda4a65c6fb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-939ab4ac-b0eb-5583-a507-30ec715ed593" :answer/id #uuid "939ab4ac-b0eb-5583-a507-30ec715ed593" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-6fe81e21-b32f-5653-9746-86ee81aa65aa" :question/id #uuid "6fe81e21-b32f-5653-9746-86ee81aa65aa" :question/math-academy-id "q-74146" :question/problem "Normalize the vector $x=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "To normalize a vector $x,$ we have to divide the vector by its norm: $\\frac{x}{‖x‖}.$ Therefore, to normalize $x,$ we first calculate $‖x‖$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖x‖ & =\\sqrt{{x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}+{x}_{3}^{2}+{x}_{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+{4}^{2}+(-1)^{2}+{1}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{0+16+1+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{18} \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we divide $x$ by its length:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x}{‖x‖} & =\\frac{x}{3\\sqrt{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3\\sqrt{2}}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3\\sqrt{2}}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ \\frac{4}{3\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{-1}{3\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{3\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ \\frac{2\\sqrt{2}}{3} \\\\ -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{6} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{6}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-9bbd8ab4-1a40-599a-b247-4e701aa93341"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-9bbd8ab4-1a40-599a-b247-4e701aa93341" :answer-field/id #uuid "9bbd8ab4-1a40-599a-b247-4e701aa93341" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-95b4a85b-7861-5ab1-b592-7b9c8569104e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-7d42fa43-344e-5abb-8870-37969fd0327c" "answer-95b4a85b-7861-5ab1-b592-7b9c8569104e" "answer-12ff338b-c3cb-5873-97ee-33513fecbc83" "answer-9f3d4087-3766-5495-930d-d4cde087cd64" "answer-5363f39a-7b6b-5cdc-aac6-d7bb396071fa"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-7d42fa43-344e-5abb-8870-37969fd0327c" :answer/id #uuid "7d42fa43-344e-5abb-8870-37969fd0327c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-95b4a85b-7861-5ab1-b592-7b9c8569104e" :answer/id #uuid "95b4a85b-7861-5ab1-b592-7b9c8569104e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ \\frac{2\\sqrt{2}}{3} \\\\ -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{6} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{6}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-12ff338b-c3cb-5873-97ee-33513fecbc83" :answer/id #uuid "12ff338b-c3cb-5873-97ee-33513fecbc83" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ \\frac{2\\sqrt{2}}{9} \\\\ -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{6} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{6}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9f3d4087-3766-5495-930d-d4cde087cd64" :answer/id #uuid "9f3d4087-3766-5495-930d-d4cde087cd64" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ \\frac{4\\sqrt{2}}{3} \\\\ -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{6} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{6}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5363f39a-7b6b-5cdc-aac6-d7bb396071fa" :answer/id #uuid "5363f39a-7b6b-5cdc-aac6-d7bb396071fa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3} \\\\ -\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{3}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-a75afdb8-44f8-53fc-b291-78342131f3c9" :question/id #uuid "a75afdb8-44f8-53fc-b291-78342131f3c9" :question/math-academy-id "q-39214" :question/problem "Normalize the vector $x=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "To normalize a vector $x,$ we have to divide the vector by its norm: $\\frac{x}{‖x‖}.$ Therefore, to normalize $x,$ we first calculate $‖x‖$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖x‖ & =\\sqrt{{x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-3)^{2}+{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{9+16} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25} \\\\  & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we divide $x$ by its length:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{x}{‖x‖} & =\\frac{x}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{3}{5} \\\\ \\frac{4}{5}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-345e93ff-6b1b-5f17-8b83-e12e5dd0c0e9"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-345e93ff-6b1b-5f17-8b83-e12e5dd0c0e9" :answer-field/id #uuid "345e93ff-6b1b-5f17-8b83-e12e5dd0c0e9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-fc6c5edb-e824-599e-8dcd-560b7fd15d07" :answer-field/choices ["answer-0301abe0-3c1d-5d0f-ba9c-e0b6f7e434e4" "answer-efe33107-6321-59f2-b121-c7a5244686c3" "answer-83177d3a-3f74-52df-b248-5042f061441e" "answer-fc6c5edb-e824-599e-8dcd-560b7fd15d07" "answer-f6855b45-5b87-54e0-b650-401ac55c3818"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0301abe0-3c1d-5d0f-ba9c-e0b6f7e434e4" :answer/id #uuid "0301abe0-3c1d-5d0f-ba9c-e0b6f7e434e4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ \\frac{4}{3}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-efe33107-6321-59f2-b121-c7a5244686c3" :answer/id #uuid "efe33107-6321-59f2-b121-c7a5244686c3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-83177d3a-3f74-52df-b248-5042f061441e" :answer/id #uuid "83177d3a-3f74-52df-b248-5042f061441e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{3}{4} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fc6c5edb-e824-599e-8dcd-560b7fd15d07" :answer/id #uuid "fc6c5edb-e824-599e-8dcd-560b7fd15d07" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{3}{5} \\\\ \\frac{4}{5}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f6855b45-5b87-54e0-b650-401ac55c3818" :answer/id #uuid "f6855b45-5b87-54e0-b650-401ac55c3818" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{5}{3} \\\\ \\frac{5}{4}\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-48de0343-fd7b-5b5e-947b-c8f60a378766" :question/id #uuid "48de0343-fd7b-5b5e-947b-c8f60a378766" :question/math-academy-id "q-39217" :question/problem "Let $x=[\\begin{aligned}k \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -2k\\end{aligned}]$ and $y=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ k \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$ Find $k$, if the distance between the vectors is $\\text{d}(x,y)=\\sqrt{83}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we calculate the distance between $x$ and $y$ in terms of $k:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}(x,y) & =‖x-y‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{({x}_{1}-{y}_{1})^{2}+({x}_{2}-{y}_{2})^{2}+({x}_{3}-{y}_{3})^{2}+({x}_{4}-{y}_{4})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(k-0)^{2}+(0-k)^{2}+((-1)-(-2))^{2}+(-2k-2)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{k}^{2}+{k}^{2}+{1}^{2}+4{k}^{2}+8k+4} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{6{k}^{2}+8k+5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the given equation  $\\text{d}(x,y)=\\sqrt{83},$ we obtain an equation that we can solve for $k:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{6{k}^{2}+8k+5} & =\\sqrt{83} \\\\ {(\\sqrt{6{k}^{2}+8k+5})}^{2} & ={(\\sqrt{83})}^{2} \\\\ 6{k}^{2}+8k+5 & =83 \\\\ 6{k}^{2}+8k-78 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the quadratic formula, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}k & =\\frac{-b\\pm \\sqrt{{b}^{2}-4ac}}{2a} \\\\  & =\\frac{-8\\pm \\sqrt{{8}^{2}-4(6)(-78)}}{2(6)} \\\\  & =\\frac{-8\\pm \\sqrt{1\\,936}}{12} \\\\  & =\\frac{-8\\pm 44}{12} \\\\  & =\\frac{-2\\pm 11}{3},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives $k=3$ and $k=-\\frac{13}{3}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-912ad5bd-997a-59d4-b69f-476bb7146fb8"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-912ad5bd-997a-59d4-b69f-476bb7146fb8" :answer-field/id #uuid "912ad5bd-997a-59d4-b69f-476bb7146fb8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-bd3f7134-17d2-5d78-a50f-aff7eb574083" :answer-field/choices ["answer-45349ee6-73ff-5b94-9038-869af5c09fbe" "answer-2dbcc1cb-9046-562f-a250-6641a5b9d78b" "answer-bd3f7134-17d2-5d78-a50f-aff7eb574083" "answer-0b0ef00b-610f-581a-8e67-24f68a95faf0" "answer-cbd1773b-2c2f-504a-b609-076b063e899c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-45349ee6-73ff-5b94-9038-869af5c09fbe" :answer/id #uuid "45349ee6-73ff-5b94-9038-869af5c09fbe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "k=-13,3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2dbcc1cb-9046-562f-a250-6641a5b9d78b" :answer/id #uuid "2dbcc1cb-9046-562f-a250-6641a5b9d78b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "k=2\\pm \\sqrt{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bd3f7134-17d2-5d78-a50f-aff7eb574083" :answer/id #uuid "bd3f7134-17d2-5d78-a50f-aff7eb574083" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "k=3,-\\frac{13}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0b0ef00b-610f-581a-8e67-24f68a95faf0" :answer/id #uuid "0b0ef00b-610f-581a-8e67-24f68a95faf0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "k=3\\pm \\sqrt{13}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cbd1773b-2c2f-504a-b609-076b063e899c" :answer/id #uuid "cbd1773b-2c2f-504a-b609-076b063e899c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "k=6,15" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-9c46599f-15c6-531f-94db-06b03ec04f84" :question/id #uuid "9c46599f-15c6-531f-94db-06b03ec04f84" :question/math-academy-id "q-74149" :question/problem "Find $k$, if $u=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ \\frac{1}{4} \\\\ \\frac{3}{4} \\\\ \\frac{k}{4}\\end{aligned}]$ is a unit vector." :question/worked-solution "First, we calculate the norm of the vector $u$ in terms of $k:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖u‖ & =\\sqrt{{u}_{1}^{2}+{u}_{2}^{2}+{u}_{3}^{2}+{u}_{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{(-\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}+{(\\frac{1}{4})}^{2}+{(\\frac{3}{4})}^{2}+{(\\frac{k}{4})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{4}+\\frac{1}{16}+\\frac{9}{16}+\\frac{{k}^{2}}{16}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{14+{k}^{2}}{16}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the given equation  $‖u‖=1,$ we obtain an equation that we can solve for $k:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{\\frac{14+{k}^{2}}{16}} & =1 \\\\ \\sqrt{14+{k}^{2}} & =4 \\\\ {(\\sqrt{14+{k}^{2}})}^{2} & ={4}^{2} \\\\ 14+{k}^{2} & =16 \\\\ {k}^{2} & =2 \\\\ k & =\\pm \\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-f00c50c9-3345-5470-8ccb-bce50ca0fdd4"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f00c50c9-3345-5470-8ccb-bce50ca0fdd4" :answer-field/id #uuid "f00c50c9-3345-5470-8ccb-bce50ca0fdd4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-eb9e68d1-fabf-5d62-b704-62d032286855" :answer-field/choices ["answer-75b1fa49-49da-5f37-8dfa-465fb4af4967" "answer-86977b64-b6c8-5365-bf6e-5ff5b06feb84" "answer-ac4581c9-0b61-577e-b7a9-aba7bac04110" "answer-eb9e68d1-fabf-5d62-b704-62d032286855" "answer-e3efac19-7b5c-5684-8e8f-127af8b3a1dd"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-75b1fa49-49da-5f37-8dfa-465fb4af4967" :answer/id #uuid "75b1fa49-49da-5f37-8dfa-465fb4af4967" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "k=\\pm 2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-86977b64-b6c8-5365-bf6e-5ff5b06feb84" :answer/id #uuid "86977b64-b6c8-5365-bf6e-5ff5b06feb84" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "k=\\pm 3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ac4581c9-0b61-577e-b7a9-aba7bac04110" :answer/id #uuid "ac4581c9-0b61-577e-b7a9-aba7bac04110" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "k=\\pm 4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-eb9e68d1-fabf-5d62-b704-62d032286855" :answer/id #uuid "eb9e68d1-fabf-5d62-b704-62d032286855" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "k=\\pm \\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e3efac19-7b5c-5684-8e8f-127af8b3a1dd" :answer/id #uuid "e3efac19-7b5c-5684-8e8f-127af8b3a1dd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "k=\\pm \\sqrt{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-d68ac222-1a16-5cb9-b7e0-2d9347a41d3b" :question/id #uuid "d68ac222-1a16-5cb9-b7e0-2d9347a41d3b" :question/math-academy-id "q-39245" :question/problem "Let $x=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 2k \\\\ -5 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].$ Find $k$, if $‖x‖=3\\sqrt{6}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we calculate the norm of the vector $x$ in terms of $k:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖x‖ & =\\sqrt{{x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}+{x}_{3}^{2}+{x}_{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+(2k)^{2}+(-5)^{2}+(-3)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4+4{k}^{2}+25+9} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4{k}^{2}+38}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the given equation  $‖x‖=3\\sqrt{6},$ we obtain an equation that we can solve for $k:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{4{k}^{2}+38} & =3\\sqrt{6} \\\\ {(\\sqrt{4{k}^{2}+38})}^{2} & ={(3\\sqrt{6})}^{2} \\\\ 4{k}^{2}+38 & =9\\cdot 6 \\\\ 4{k}^{2} & =16 \\\\ {k}^{2} & =4 \\\\ k & =\\pm 2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-02ef7ff6-0500-5b8b-a917-caba50da13f7"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-02ef7ff6-0500-5b8b-a917-caba50da13f7" :answer-field/id #uuid "02ef7ff6-0500-5b8b-a917-caba50da13f7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-14038965-93fb-5337-922f-f6687215b2ee" :answer-field/choices ["answer-14038965-93fb-5337-922f-f6687215b2ee" "answer-a77c702c-0670-52cc-921b-8144c5fc6def" "answer-5f9be16a-c316-5442-bc8b-8cfb7408be8b" "answer-af05c26e-f58f-5aee-81d1-128eb4950787" "answer-f27ae383-4a84-5468-bd31-55d4a78a6a5f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-14038965-93fb-5337-922f-f6687215b2ee" :answer/id #uuid "14038965-93fb-5337-922f-f6687215b2ee" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "k=\\pm 2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a77c702c-0670-52cc-921b-8144c5fc6def" :answer/id #uuid "a77c702c-0670-52cc-921b-8144c5fc6def" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "k=\\pm 2\\sqrt{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-5f9be16a-c316-5442-bc8b-8cfb7408be8b" :answer/id #uuid "5f9be16a-c316-5442-bc8b-8cfb7408be8b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "k=\\pm 4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-af05c26e-f58f-5aee-81d1-128eb4950787" :answer/id #uuid "af05c26e-f58f-5aee-81d1-128eb4950787" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "k=\\pm 6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f27ae383-4a84-5468-bd31-55d4a78a6a5f" :answer/id #uuid "f27ae383-4a84-5468-bd31-55d4a78a6a5f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "k=\\pm \\sqrt{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186135031 :tutorial/content "The vector space $\\mathbb{R}^n,$ paired with the dot product, is called a **Euclidean space**. \n\nFor a vector ![](images/83/838ca0a3284985fa58d5ac894740b15f9bbbfd931299834cc8e062e364bbf983.svg) in $\\mathbb{R}^n,$  the **norm** (or **length**)  is given by \n\n$$\n\\Vert \\mathbf{x} \\Vert = \\sqrt{\\mathbf{x} \\cdot \\mathbf{x}} = \\sqrt{x_1^2+x_2^2+\\ldots+x_n^2}.\n$$\n\nFor example, consider the vector ![](images/2a/2a4e0070bdec6033ab8b71cbb77dbd8569bea8672c0e17cedbf876a77ce56bb2.svg) The norm of this vector is calculated as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖x‖ & =\\sqrt{{x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-5)^{2}+(12)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25+144} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{169} \\\\  & =13.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that the dot product of a vector with itself is always non-negative, $\\mathbf{x}\\cdot\\mathbf{x}\\geq 0,$ so it's always possible to take the square root $\\sqrt{ \\mathbf{x}\\cdot\\mathbf{x} }.$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186135073 :tutorial/content "In a Euclidean space, the **distance** between the vectors $\\mathbf{x}$ and $\\mathbf{y}$ is the norm of the difference $\\mathbf{x}-\\mathbf{y},$ that is\n\n$$\n\\text{d}(\\mathbf{x}, \\mathbf{y}) = \\Vert \\mathbf{x} - \\mathbf{y} \\Vert.\n$$\n\nTo create a formula for the distance, we write the vectors in component form:\n![](images/01/011499b685af9a4c78d195755dc34e7b0d6ea0292eb2e9feafb94312fc7ee4b3.svg) \n\nNow, we can express the norm in terms of the components:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}(x,y) & =‖x-y‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{({x}_{1}-{y}_{1})^{2}+({x}_{2}-{y}_{2})^{2}+⋯+({x}_{n}-{y}_{n})^{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor example, we can use the formula to find the distance between the vectors ![](images/2e/2e5d7cbac29024ca7f343363598714ea17bb180036d2f50f094a25584be2e23e.svg) and ![](images/37/37364e71c36f25701aa2e3b0ad368d4567b5719aa0c884ff0406ee9686125808.svg) as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}(x,y) & =‖x-y‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{({x}_{1}-{y}_{1})^{2}+({x}_{2}-{y}_{2})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(1-(-5))^{2}+(4-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{6}^{2}+{3}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{45} \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186135074 :tutorial/content "We can factor a constant out of the norm, provided that we take the absolute value of the constant:\n\n$$\n\\Vert k \\mathbf{x} \\Vert= \\vert k \\vert \\cdot \\Vert \\mathbf{x} \\Vert\n$$\n\nFor example, consider the vector ![](images/43/430769431d512b87b6e67712fd8bd8de3802688f883600602a0d45b2749089cc.svg) To compute the norm of a multiple of $\\mathbf{x},$ say ${\\color{blue}-2}\\mathbf{x},$ we can factor the absolute value $|{\\color{blue}-2}|$ out of the norm as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖-2x‖ & =|-2|\\cdot ‖x‖ \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\sqrt{{x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}} \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\sqrt{{3}^{2}+{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\sqrt{9+16} \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\sqrt{25} \\\\  & =2\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Note:** We can verify that we'd get the same result if we multiplied the $\\color{blue}-2$ first, before computing the norm. Multiplying by ${\\color{blue}-2},$ we have\n\n![](images/5d/5da07173bda8f167d9a0609457fd10f1e3fdcdd2de498fd08c1c0035a205e5e1.svg)\n\nThen, computing the norm, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖-2x‖ & =\\sqrt{{x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-6)^{2}+(-8)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{36+64} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{100} \\\\  & =10.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:tutorial/validate]} {:db/id 17592186133982 :activity/expected-seconds 480.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]}]
